File: lib/OCP/Cmd/SSH.pm:75-79

```perl
my $cp_spec = $spec->{control_planes};
if ($node_arg eq 'police1' || $node_arg =~ /^police\d+$/ || $node_arg =~ /^cp/) {
    if ($cp_spec->{provider} eq 'ssh') {
```

`$spec->{control_planes}` is the raw `ocp.yaml` field, which OCP::Config always treats as an arrayref (see _compact_control_planes and `cps->[0] // {}` in OCP::Cmd::Apply::Bootstrap::cp_identity). Dereferencing it as a hash throws `Not a HASH reference at lib/OCP/Cmd/SSH.pm line 79.` and bypasses the helpful `_unknown_node_error` path on line 92. Use `$cp_spec->[0]{provider}` instead.

Repro:
1. Set control_planes in ocp.yaml to a list of multiple CPs (mixed hetzner+ssh is the canonical case).
2. ocp ssh --node police1
Observed: process dies with "Not a HASH reference" before the unknown-node handler can run.
